      "normalized_sha256": "0fb133ff75575a0ee6fcbacc98616795344d89d1565fda789fc5aabc0089ca80",
      "rationale": "This is the nonpositive base equation defining oddDigitsProduct as the empty product.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-0fb133ff75575a0ee6fcbacc98616795344d89d1565fda789fc5aabc0089ca80",
      "start_line": 19,
      "text": "  rule oddDigitsProduct(N) => 1\n    requires N <=Int 0"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 25,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "1041526ea39d2526c2c36596926e2630a1c4b9a747e782f19bb0b629f8b0c133",
      "rationale": "This is the guarded odd-positive recurrence defining oddDigitsProduct by multiplying the last decimal digit and recursing on the remaining prefix.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-1041526ea39d2526c2c36596926e2630a1c4b9a747e782f19bb0b629f8b0c133",
      "start_line": 21,
      "text": "  rule oddDigitsProduct(N)\n    => pyMod(N, 10) *Int\n       oddDigitsProduct((N -Int pyMod(N, 10)) /Int 10)\n    requires N >Int 0\n     andBool pyMod(N, 2) ==Int 1"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 29,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "52cf77b863948207a5ea8f92c48af09fa4ea2f6e6837a10fcd27522d55925142",
      "rationale": "This is the guarded even-positive recurrence defining oddDigitsProduct by discarding the even last digit and recursing on the remaining prefix.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-52cf77b863948207a5ea8f92c48af09fa4ea2f6e6837a10fcd27522d55925142",
      "start_line": 26,
      "text": "  rule oddDigitsProduct(N)\n    => oddDigitsProduct((N -Int pyMod(N, 10)) /Int 10)\n    requires N >Int 0\n     andBool pyMod(N, 2) ==Int 0"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 32,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "fb10643f487bf1c3216e86d1e8932d17f6f1bc2a84f17f452affaf4bd7dc8983",
      "rationale": "This is the nonpositive base equation defining oddDigitSeen to be zero before any positive decimal digit is examined.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-fb10643f487bf1c3216e86d1e8932d17f6f1bc2a84f17f452affaf4bd7dc8983",
      "start_line": 31,
      "text": "  rule oddDigitSeen(N) => 0\n    requires N <=Int 0"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 35,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "6fefbc74e7cfb69f05c31ea4a791697a7f52aab7b42b868079f71ea86b367ecb",
      "rationale": "This is the guarded odd-positive defining equation for oddDigitSeen, returning one when the current decimal digit is odd.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-6fefbc74e7cfb69f05c31ea4a791697a7f52aab7b42b868079f71ea86b367ecb",
      "start_line": 33,
      "text": "  rule oddDigitSeen(N) => 1\n    requires N >Int 0\n     andBool pyMod(N, 2) ==Int 1"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 39,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "8cb33ca21099712b8c8b52cf660c4841a997bbd1e12caf5367ac795c0253f9fa",
      "rationale": "This is the guarded even-positive recurrence defining oddDigitSeen by continuing with the remaining decimal prefix.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-8cb33ca21099712b8c8b52cf660c4841a997bbd1e12caf5367ac795c0253f9fa",
      "start_line": 36,
      "text": "  rule oddDigitSeen(N)\n    => oddDigitSeen((N -Int pyMod(N, 10)) /Int 10)\n    requires N >Int 0\n     andBool pyMod(N, 2) ==Int 0"
    }
  ],
